set -eu
# The same lane as `stall`, with the same forty-minute-old transcript and the same live row, against
# a host that was asleep for thirty-two of those forty minutes. Nothing here is a stall: the session
# has not stopped working, it has not been running, and D-008's thirty minutes were written about
# unchanged transcripts on a machine that was there to change them.
#
# What the scenario asserts is an absence — no `stall` line and no Mac message — so the two things
# that could make it pass for the wrong reason are worth naming. The row carries a pid, so the lane
# is in flight rather than rowless and the crash rule never sees it; and the marker is a minute old,
# so no gap is reported and the only `pmset` read in `calls.log` is the stall rule making this
# judgement.
"$BATON" tick
